// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Source File : scripts/SpawnDefs/V_PvP_05_01/_src/V_PvP_05_01_NPCs.xls 	Sheet : RV_Hero_Heavy_Info 
//
// Script      : Xlstospawndef.bat 
// Version     : 31 
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Script Variable Greeting :
"P4100746863" "<em=lecture f=a>Hey, {HeroName}. Welcome to Recluse's Victory.  You're in for the ride of your life.<em none>"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P2354959956" "<em=clipboard f=a>Ah, good, {HeroName}.  You're here.  Let's get started.<em=none>"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P2922589884" "<em=lecture f=a>The battle is about to begin, {HeroName}.   You up for it?<em=none>"
// Script Variable RestrictedText :
"P1236112706" "Beat it, scum.  I don't talk to Villains."
// Script Variable InfoText :
"P338871980" "There are two pieces of important technology I want to discuss with you.  Let me break them down:<br><br><b><color orange>Heavy Support Robot</b></color><br><br>This little number behind me is something we wish we'd had during the Rikti Invasion.  This is the new Freedom Corps Cataphract Class Heavy Assault Robot, or 'Heavy' for short.  Think of it as a walking tank.<br><br>There are three Heavy platform stations, like the ones you see behind me, in Atlas Park.  To take command of a Heavy, simply touch the control panel.  This will only work when a Heavy is on the platform.<br><br>Now this is important to remember.  The Heavies are slow movers so if you want its benefits, you will have to stick close to it.<br><br>Arachnos has a version of a Heavy, too, so be careful.<br><br><b><color orange>Temporal Anchors aka 'Pillboxes'</b></color><br><br>There are seven Temporal Anchors located throughout the city, although all the soldiers just call them 'pillboxes'.  <br><br>These pillboxes have a four-turret security system and may appear in different states depending on who has ownership of them.<br><br>To capture a pillbox, defeat the turrets and then activate the control panel in the center.  Once activated, a defense shield will activate and protect you.  You will also have control of all four turrets for as long as you stay in the center of the pillbox.  These babies can really reach out and touch someone!<br><br>If you leave the pillbox you will no longer be able to direct their fire.  However, you can bring them back into your command by re-accessing the control panel.  If you leave, any Hero can take over the turrets while the pillbox is under our possession."
// Script Variable OutLoudInfoText :
"P664526768" "<em=clipboard><em=none>"
// Script Variable Leave :
// DisplayName for N_Scientist :
"P1487019530" "D.A.T.A. Tech Congreves"

// ************************************************************************
// ************************************************************************
// ************************************************************************

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Generated by transModule
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Source File : scripts/SpawnDefs/V_PvP_05_01/_src/V_PvP_05_01_NPCs.xls 	Sheet : RV_Hero_PvP_Info 
//
// Script      : Xlstospawndef.bat 
// Version     : 31 
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Script Variable Greeting :
"P2358926279" "<em=lecture f=a>Hey, {HeroName}. Good to see you.  Let me explain how all this works.<em=none>"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P2513681085" "<em=wave f=a>{HeroName}, let's talk about what you'll be doing here.<em=none>"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P1859453398" "<em=lecture f=a>Excellent.  You're here.  Let's get started, {HeroName}.<em=none>"
// Script Variable RestrictedText :
"P1401560512" "Security!!  Villain alert!"
// Script Variable InfoText :
"P2534886927" "{HeroName}!  On behalf of the Freedom Corps and Statesman, thank you for joining in what could be <b>the</b> most important battle of our lifetimes.  Here's the situation:<br><br>Topside there are seven pillboxes that serve as temporal time anchors placed throughout the city.  You can see them on the Ops Map behind me, marked as white crosses.  Each time Heroes capture a pillbox it sets the world back to the way it ought to be.  These captures, and the areas afffected, are updated live on the map here:  <color blue>blue</color> for Heroes and <color red>red</color> for Villains.<br><br>We must capture 6 pillboxes to reset the proper order of time.  Be advised that, even then, the hold will only be temporary.  We are still hoping for a way to lock it down, so be diligent.  Once the area is secured, you will then take the fight directly to the villains. We will be tracking your actions and will reward you for your bravery. <br><br>You are not alone in this fight, hero.  The Freedom Phalanx and even Statesman himself is here for support when needed.  We also have some new technologies to add to your arsenal.  Talk to <color yellow>D.A.T.A. Tech Congreves</color> standing near those robots to learn more.<br><br>If you wish to join the battle now, use the Portal at the west end of this room.  The future depends on you so good luck!"
// Script Variable OutLoudInfoText :
"P376970871" "<em=at_ease><em=none>"
// Script Variable Leave :
// DisplayName for N_Scientist :
"P2584330870" "Commander Murat"

