// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Source File : scripts/SpawnDefs/V_PvP_05_01/_src/V_PvP_05_01_NPCs.xls 	Sheet : RV_Villain_PvP_Info 
//
// Script      : Xlstospawndef.bat 
// Version     : 31 
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Script Variable Greeting :
"P3117421432" "<em=lecture f=a>Over here, {VillainName}.<em none>"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P1629338480" "Let's get started, {VillainName}."
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P3218730614" "<em=lecture f=a>Over here, {VillainName}.<em=none>"
// Script Variable RestrictedText :
"P502268531" "I don't deal with heroes.  And you're dead meat."
// Script Variable InfoText :
"P4282999033" "{VillainName}!  Let me apprise you of the situation.  <br><br>Topside, there are seven pillboxes that serve as Temporal Anchors placed throughout the city.  You can see them on the Ops Map wall, marked as white crosses.  Each time we capture a pillbox, it sets the world one step closer to Lord Recluse's dream.  These captures, and the areas affected, are updated live on the map here:  <color red>red</color> for Villains and <color blue>blue</color> for Heroes.  <br><br>We must capture 6 pillboxes to bring our destiny to reality.  Be advised that, even when we succeed, the hold is only temporary.  We are working on a way to lock it down, so be diligent.  Once the area is secured, you must then take the fight directly to the Heroes!  We will be tracking your actions and will reward you for your dedication.<br><br>You are not alone in this fight, soldier.  All of the Patrons and even Lord Recluse himself will be supporting the battle.  We also have some new technologies to add to your arsenal.  Talk to <color yellow>Arbiter Minos</color> on the first floor of the Teleporter room to learn more.  <br><br>If you want to join the battle now, use the Portal directly behind this Ops Map.<br><br>Remember:  power in unity!  Obey and win!"
// Script Variable OutLoudInfoText :
// Script Variable Leave :
// DisplayName for N_Scientist :
"P568614682" "Arbiter Uller"

